{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1336800-characters-inspired-by-movies-and-tv","id":1336800,"title":"Characters inspired by movies and TV","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-19T01:39:45-07:00","id":1336800,"title":"Characters inspired by movies and TV","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"> Some activity in a subreddit made me think of something.<br /> <i>Please tell us a character you want to run that is inspired by a bit of business from a movie or TV show. Please post a link to an example.</i><br /> I'll go first.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lPMSGTfK4Aw\" target=\"_blank\">I want to run a Wraith the Oblivion character based on Large Marge</a>.<br /> Now, you have a go.<br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T14:57:31-07:00","id":1336948,"title":"","content":"Is this just for the purpose of PCs we want to play, or can we include NPCs for games we are storytelling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T16:30:56-07:00","id":1336959,"title":"","content":"Either, or even something else. I started the thread in the spirit of fun - just keep it fun and link to a video to cite the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T11:57:57-07:00","id":1337130,"title":"","content":"I ran a Changeling game last year with a few characters lifted almost directly from this movie: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hjYtwGdK_48\" target=\"_blank\">Shopping</a><br /> <br /> Jude Law's character was the inspiration for both the leader of a gang of teenage Changelings and a Vampire street criminal, Sadie Frost's character was the inspiration for a street Mage, Sean Bean's character became a criminal Ventrue Elder, and Sean Pertwee inspired another street Mage who was the mentor for the Sadie Frost inspired character.<br /> <br /> So one movie brought forth five major characters or NPCs - that's pretty good going!<br /> <br /> p.s. It also has a brief appearance by a young British actor you might have heard of: Jason Isaacs<br /> p.p.s. IT's also well worth watching if you get a chance, very rare to see that many talented actors in the early part of their careers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}